14. Interview Explanation (1-minute version)

We scan the array once while maintaining the minimum stock price seen so far.
For every current price, we compute the profit if we sold today after buying at that minimum price.
We update the maximum profit whenever this profit is larger.
If we encounter a new lower price, we update the minimum.
This guarantees that buying always happens before selling.
The algorithm runs in O(n) time and O(1) space.
